WEBVTT

00:09.300 --> 00:10.135
Conny!

00:10.468 --> 00:11.594
Are there any survivors?

00:13.138 --> 00:13.972
No.

00:15.473 --> 00:16.307
None at all.

00:18.018 --> 00:19.185
It's all over.

00:20.270 --> 00:23.273
My hometown. It's gone forever.

00:30.864 --> 00:32.782
Hey! Something's strange here.

00:35.869 --> 00:37.370
Has anyone spotted any bodies?

00:38.621 --> 00:39.456
No.

00:40.123 --> 00:41.082
I haven't.

00:41.583 --> 00:43.001
How is that even possible?

00:43.543 --> 00:45.545
Titans come
and not a single drop of blood--

00:45.628 --> 00:46.921
Everyone must have escaped!

00:47.297 --> 00:50.717
It means nobody here was eaten.
Including your family.

00:51.926 --> 00:54.304
I see. That's got to be it!

00:54.804 --> 00:57.182
Yes. It's unbelievable to think
that Titans ate everyone

00:57.265 --> 01:00.185
without leaving blood behind.

01:01.227 --> 01:03.229
It's not all that's unbelievable.

01:04.731 --> 01:07.901
If the entire village was evacuated,

01:08.860 --> 01:10.779
why would Titans smash these houses

01:11.446 --> 01:13.865
with nobody in them?

01:15.283 --> 01:18.870
But what really boggles my mind
is the stables.

01:20.246 --> 01:21.748
If they tried to escape without horses,

01:22.290 --> 01:24.834
their chances of survival would be slim.

01:26.419 --> 01:27.837
Everyone got their torches?

01:28.546 --> 01:29.422
Let's move!

01:29.923 --> 01:32.592
Our mission now is to locate
and assess the breach in the wall!

01:33.009 --> 01:33.885
Yes, sir!

01:44.479 --> 01:47.190
Welcome home.

02:02.789 --> 02:03.790
Just now...

02:05.291 --> 02:06.459
Conny, hurry up!

02:06.876 --> 02:08.461
We're falling behind Gerger!

02:09.963 --> 02:12.674
Reiner? Did you hear that? The Titan--

02:12.757 --> 02:14.425
I didn't hear anything at all.

02:15.760 --> 02:18.429
Enough with the chit-chat.
Focus on the mission!

02:19.013 --> 02:20.431
But it... I think...

02:21.224 --> 02:22.433
I don't know how, but...

02:23.017 --> 02:23.893
I think...

02:24.686 --> 02:26.271
-My mom--
-Conny!

02:26.563 --> 02:28.606
Do you understand the situation we're in?

02:29.816 --> 02:34.154
Hundreds of thousands of lives depend on
whether we complete this mission or not!

02:35.071 --> 02:38.199
Your family might have escaped,
but it's not over yet!

02:38.908 --> 02:40.702
If you're a soldier,
put the mission first!

02:45.331 --> 02:47.709
Yes. Good point.

02:49.961 --> 02:51.045
He's right!

04:34.774 --> 04:36.025
7 HOURS AFTER DISCOVERING THE TITAN

04:36.109 --> 04:37.652
We're getting close to the wall now,

04:37.860 --> 04:39.529
so there are no people living in the area.

04:40.446 --> 04:43.116
Right. It didn't take us very long.

04:45.743 --> 04:47.704
All right, let's head to the south.

04:49.247 --> 04:50.206
What for?

04:51.040 --> 04:53.334
There shouldn't be any villages
south of here.

04:54.377 --> 04:57.213
We need to find the location
where the wall was breached.

04:57.755 --> 05:00.216
We'll ride along the wall from the west
until we find it.

05:01.551 --> 05:04.137
But Christa and I
don't have our battle gear.

05:04.804 --> 05:07.974
There are probably Titans
roaming everywhere in the south.

05:08.391 --> 05:11.227
It's very possible
that we'll become Titan food.

05:12.395 --> 05:14.397
Let the two of us withdraw from the front.

05:15.732 --> 05:16.566
Ymir.

05:16.733 --> 05:20.278
You can't. I'll need somebody
to send a report.

05:21.029 --> 05:24.407
I know how you feel,
but you signed up for this as a soldier.

05:30.955 --> 05:31.789
Ymir.

05:32.373 --> 05:34.667
I'm fine with putting my life on the line.

05:36.836 --> 05:40.465
After all, I'm the one who chose
to join the Scouts.

05:41.674 --> 05:44.052
But it's not the same for you.

05:45.887 --> 05:48.264
The only reason you joined the Scouts
was that--

05:48.347 --> 05:51.184
Shut up! Do you think I did it for you?

05:51.934 --> 05:53.686
Then why are you even here?

05:54.562 --> 05:58.024
You kept trying to convince me
to join the Military Police.

05:58.232 --> 05:59.901
But then you gave that privilege to me!

06:01.861 --> 06:05.740
There's no way I'm good enough
to make the top ten on skill alone.

06:06.657 --> 06:07.784
I'm sure if I asked anyone,

06:08.117 --> 06:10.536
they'd say you deserved to be in it,
not me.

06:11.662 --> 06:13.372
I don't know how you did it, but...

06:15.541 --> 06:16.375
Why?

06:17.335 --> 06:18.836
Why would you go that far for me?

06:23.591 --> 06:24.467
Does it...

06:26.302 --> 06:28.012
have to do with my family?

06:30.807 --> 06:32.767
Yes, it does.

06:35.311 --> 06:36.187
Christa.

06:37.146 --> 06:38.314
Don't worry about it.

06:39.524 --> 06:43.736
I'm only here for myself and nothing else.

06:46.280 --> 06:47.323
I see.

06:50.785 --> 06:51.786
Thank goodness.

06:59.794 --> 07:03.756
9 HOURS AFTER THE TITAN DISCOVERY
EASTERN DEFENSIVE LINE

07:06.259 --> 07:08.177
The target is within range!

07:08.678 --> 07:10.930
All cannons, prepare to fire!

07:12.640 --> 07:14.767
Not yet! Wait for the order!

07:15.476 --> 07:16.310
Sir!

07:17.228 --> 07:18.604
Fire!

07:38.499 --> 07:39.333
Did I get it?

07:41.627 --> 07:43.296
You did it, Captain Rico!

07:43.588 --> 07:46.382
At this rate,
they'll never break our defense!

07:47.091 --> 07:50.178
No. The Titans' strength
is in their numbers.

07:51.012 --> 07:54.599
If they attack as a group,
this line won't stand a chance.

07:56.642 --> 07:58.186
But what is it?

07:59.020 --> 07:59.854
Something isn't...

08:01.856 --> 08:02.940
This is strange...

08:03.608 --> 08:05.735
Captain Hannes! Is something wrong?

08:06.569 --> 08:09.405
We haven't even spotted
a single Titan yet.

08:10.323 --> 08:12.950
We've got to be getting close
to the hole now.

08:13.784 --> 08:16.370
And yet, doesn't it seem awfully quiet
around here?

08:20.166 --> 08:24.754
Hopefully, we can sneak in and out
without causing a storm.

08:39.936 --> 08:44.607
11 HOURS AFTER THE TITAN DISCOVERY
SOUTHERN TEAM

08:46.984 --> 08:47.860
When?

08:49.862 --> 08:51.239
When will they show?

08:52.990 --> 08:54.283
When will it happen?

08:55.326 --> 08:58.371
They could leap out of the shadows
in any second.

09:00.748 --> 09:01.582
No.

09:02.667 --> 09:07.630
The closer we get to the hole,
the more inevitable it becomes.

09:09.090 --> 09:10.424
Damn it!

09:11.634 --> 09:13.177
This is driving me crazy!

09:39.120 --> 09:41.664
Did you follow the wall here, too?

09:42.123 --> 09:44.625
Yes. Where did you find the hole?

09:45.042 --> 09:45.876
What?

09:47.044 --> 09:49.505
We didn't find anything in the west.

09:50.715 --> 09:52.383
Didn't you find it on your way?

09:53.551 --> 09:54.385
No.

09:55.928 --> 09:57.513
There's no hole this way either.

10:04.520 --> 10:06.063
Is it possible we missed it?

10:06.355 --> 10:07.189
No way.

10:07.857 --> 10:10.067
We can't miss a hole
that's big enough for Titans to use.

10:10.901 --> 10:13.070
Should we go back and look again?

10:13.613 --> 10:18.200
We'll need to, but the horses
and the rest of us are exhausted.

10:19.869 --> 10:21.412
If only we had some moonlight...

10:23.581 --> 10:24.415
Yes.

10:27.835 --> 10:28.711
What's that?

10:34.008 --> 10:35.384
Castle ruins?

10:50.900 --> 10:54.820
It looks like a mess,
but we can make do with it for one night.

10:56.405 --> 10:58.908
Right. Luckily, the moon is out.

11:08.459 --> 11:09.293
Hanji.

11:11.504 --> 11:12.755
Hey, four-eyes.

11:14.465 --> 11:18.052
Are your hobbies so boring that playing
with rocks is somehow fun for you?

11:19.095 --> 11:21.055
Yes. That's right.

11:21.931 --> 11:23.516
But this is no ordinary rock.

11:24.183 --> 11:27.561
It's a hardened fragment of skin
left behind by the Female Titan.

11:28.020 --> 11:30.064
What? It didn't disappear?

11:30.523 --> 11:31.357
Right!

11:31.565 --> 11:32.650
Annie reverted from a Titan,

11:32.775 --> 11:34.985
but it's still intact,
even though it broke off her body.

11:35.569 --> 11:38.072
It didn't evaporate. It didn't disappear.

11:38.989 --> 11:40.950
So I thought, "What if?"

11:41.325 --> 11:43.077
When I compared it to a piece of the wall,

11:43.285 --> 11:46.997
its pattern and composition
were practically identical.

11:47.832 --> 11:51.043
In other words, the wall is a barricade
of humongous Titans.

11:51.419 --> 11:52.503
And if I'm right,

11:53.045 --> 11:56.257
the surface is constructed
with hardened Titan skin.

11:57.550 --> 12:00.094
That's exactly what Armin was saying...

12:02.346 --> 12:03.431
Then--

12:04.348 --> 12:06.350
Let me finish, Armin.

12:07.268 --> 12:10.771
As it stands, we'll be hard-pressed
to fill the hole in Wall Rose.

12:11.480 --> 12:14.817
That is, unless we can find
the perfect boulder to plug it.

12:16.152 --> 12:19.405
But if Eren, in his transformed state...

12:20.239 --> 12:24.410
could use the Titans' hardening ability
to seal a hole in the wall...

12:26.287 --> 12:27.288
Use me...

12:28.956 --> 12:30.291
to seal the wall?

12:32.376 --> 12:34.587
It should be made of the same material.

12:35.212 --> 12:37.548
And seeing how
the hardened section won't evaporate

12:37.840 --> 12:39.884
even after you revert from a Titan...

12:41.010 --> 12:41.844
it's possible.

12:46.056 --> 12:48.434
Trying it is well worth the risk.

12:49.393 --> 12:51.437
And assuming it does work,

12:52.229 --> 12:54.607
reclaiming Wall Maria is feasible, too.

12:55.733 --> 12:57.193
Up until now, we've had to transport

12:57.568 --> 12:59.904
a large number of materials and supplies.

13:00.321 --> 13:03.616
That's why the need for outposts
past the wall hindered our progress.

13:04.450 --> 13:07.786
But if we don't have to accommodate
supply wagons,

13:08.120 --> 13:10.331
we could quickly make our way
to Shiganshina.

13:11.290 --> 13:14.001
What if we carried out the plan at night?

13:14.460 --> 13:15.794
-At night?
-Yes.

13:16.545 --> 13:18.339
During the night, when Titans can't move.

13:20.174 --> 13:21.175
I see...

13:21.550 --> 13:25.387
If the group was small enough,
you could sneak into Wall Maria.

13:27.556 --> 13:29.892
The current situation
is already as bad as it is,

13:30.601 --> 13:32.895
but we still have a glimmer of hope.

13:34.230 --> 13:36.357
Yes, but remember...

13:37.024 --> 13:40.110
it all depends on whether
Eren can seal a hole or not.

13:42.404 --> 13:45.115
I realize asking for this
hardly seems fair, but...

13:46.367 --> 13:47.618
Do you think you can do it?

13:57.795 --> 13:59.838
It doesn't matter what you think.

14:01.298 --> 14:03.592
You have to. There's no other choice.

14:04.510 --> 14:05.761
We're out of options.

14:06.428 --> 14:10.140
Our forces are struggling so desperately,
there's nothing else they can do.

14:11.517 --> 14:12.977
You have to succeed.

14:13.727 --> 14:14.562
I will!

14:15.020 --> 14:17.606
I'll do whatever it takes
to seal the wall!

14:19.149 --> 14:20.192
Whatever it takes...

14:28.117 --> 14:28.951
The basement...

14:29.660 --> 14:31.161
My dad's basement...

14:32.037 --> 14:33.914
If what my dad said was true,

14:34.582 --> 14:37.167
we'll find the answers
to everything there.

14:45.259 --> 14:46.260
It's Ehrmich District.

15:00.941 --> 15:01.984
Hey, keep moving.

15:02.568 --> 15:03.903
You'll end up like a lost little kid.

15:05.154 --> 15:06.322
This is...

15:07.239 --> 15:09.283
What did you expect to see?

15:10.659 --> 15:12.870
This is what happens when the wall falls.

15:15.372 --> 15:18.375
Mommy! Daddy!

15:20.836 --> 15:21.712
Hey!

15:22.421 --> 15:23.714
Where do you think you're going?

15:25.090 --> 15:28.427
Take a good look at the faces of people
who have lost everything.

15:30.095 --> 15:32.723
The faces of everyone
you and your people abandoned.

15:33.933 --> 15:35.517
If your church's wish comes true,

15:36.143 --> 15:38.729
and Titans come flooding
through the walls,

15:39.647 --> 15:41.815
we'll all be gobbled up
in their stinking mouths

15:42.107 --> 15:45.819
and die in the worst way possible.

15:46.654 --> 15:48.614
All of humanity digested as one.

15:53.035 --> 15:56.038
Once we leave Ehrmich,
we'll be in Titan territory.

15:57.039 --> 15:59.124
Eren? Do you think you can ride a horse?

15:59.541 --> 16:02.127
Yes. I feel fully recovered now.

16:02.878 --> 16:04.463
Yours is ready at the west lift.

16:04.755 --> 16:05.923
-Let's hurry.
-Right.

16:09.677 --> 16:11.387
Section Commander, we should hurry.

16:12.054 --> 16:13.722
Give me a minute, Moblit.

16:15.557 --> 16:18.060
Have you had a change of heart yet?

16:23.482 --> 16:25.609
We don't have time for this!
You know, don't you?

16:26.068 --> 16:29.071
Will you talk, or won't you?
Make up your mind already!

16:30.906 --> 16:32.449
I cannot say anything.

16:33.283 --> 16:37.121
The other believers are the same as me,
and that will never change.

16:38.163 --> 16:39.665
Well, thanks for nothing!

16:40.040 --> 16:42.626
We're so grateful
for all the help you've given!

16:43.293 --> 16:48.173
It's too great a decision
for a single person to make.

16:49.466 --> 16:52.011
The Order of the Walls must always adhere
to the sacred will

16:52.094 --> 16:54.221
-we're bound to obey.
-Thank you.

16:54.972 --> 16:56.098
Whose will?

16:57.099 --> 16:58.267
God or something?

16:58.559 --> 17:00.060
I cannot say anything.

17:00.853 --> 17:03.772
However, I can tell you the name

17:04.356 --> 17:08.736
of one who is under their sacred will,
the one we were instructed to monitor.

17:09.319 --> 17:10.279
"Monitor"?

17:12.364 --> 17:16.285
That person joined the Scout Regiment
as of this year.

17:19.413 --> 17:20.706
Her name is...

17:21.457 --> 17:22.499
Excuse me!

17:23.167 --> 17:24.543
104th Cadet Corps!

17:25.210 --> 17:26.420
Sasha Braus!

17:28.589 --> 17:29.673
Her?

17:30.174 --> 17:31.091
Who's that?

17:31.258 --> 17:33.802
This is for you, Section Commander.

17:34.053 --> 17:36.013
You must find her at once.

17:36.513 --> 17:37.431
Only she...

17:37.848 --> 17:41.560
may know the truth
which even we cannot perceive.

17:42.227 --> 17:44.772
That is all the information I can share.

17:46.732 --> 17:48.817
I leave the rest in your hands.

17:49.526 --> 17:51.403
If she's in the 104th,

17:51.653 --> 17:53.197
then she's deep in the front lines
right now.

17:53.697 --> 17:54.698
Let's go!

17:55.199 --> 17:56.408
We need to hurry!

17:56.825 --> 17:57.659
Wait!

17:59.912 --> 18:00.746
Sasha?

18:01.663 --> 18:03.082
What are you doing here?

18:06.418 --> 18:09.463
Upon my arrival,
I gave my report to the Commander!

18:09.755 --> 18:11.507
Afterward, I was entrusted
to deliver this message

18:11.632 --> 18:13.092
to the Section Commander!

18:13.759 --> 18:14.676
A message?

18:15.135 --> 18:17.429
Thank you. Good work.

18:20.015 --> 18:23.060
So, who is this girl in the 104th?

18:23.477 --> 18:25.437
She's the smallest one of us.

18:26.063 --> 18:27.731
She's got long golden hair.

18:28.357 --> 18:29.900
Oh, and...

18:31.360 --> 18:32.194
She's cute.

18:34.238 --> 18:36.198
She's always hanging around Ymir.

18:37.950 --> 18:38.909
Ymir?

18:42.162 --> 18:43.455
What's the meaning of this?

18:45.791 --> 18:46.625
Ymir...

18:48.627 --> 18:49.586
you're...

18:52.005 --> 18:53.048
Everyone, wake up!

18:53.465 --> 18:55.717
Get to the tower! Quickly!

19:04.893 --> 19:07.479
I couldn't see them in the darkness,
but then the moon...

19:10.774 --> 19:13.402
How? How can they move?

19:14.153 --> 19:16.196
It's been so long since the sun set!

19:17.823 --> 19:18.949
What's going on here?

19:19.616 --> 19:21.618
Hey! Look at that!

19:23.203 --> 19:26.373
It's huge! What the hell is it? A Titan?

19:27.541 --> 19:29.168
No, it's more like...

19:29.960 --> 19:31.170
It's like a beast!

19:32.171 --> 19:33.088
Right?

19:37.759 --> 19:39.887
It's headed for the wall!

19:47.352 --> 19:49.605
-Does everyone understand?
-Yes!

19:51.273 --> 19:53.483
-We've got to go!
-Calm down, Eren.

19:55.736 --> 19:56.904
You all listen, too.

19:57.779 --> 19:59.281
We're going our separate ways now.

19:59.907 --> 20:01.158
The rest is up to you.

20:02.326 --> 20:04.661
Erwin may have thrown you together
with your squad,

20:05.329 --> 20:07.289
but everything's riding on you.

20:08.081 --> 20:09.833
Got it, Armin?

20:10.209 --> 20:12.753
Work with Hanji
and combine your knowledge.

20:13.170 --> 20:14.338
Yes, sir!

20:15.214 --> 20:16.089
Mikasa.

20:16.798 --> 20:19.301
I don't know
why you're so attached to Eren...

20:20.302 --> 20:23.805
but use the utmost of your ability
to protect him at all costs.

20:24.223 --> 20:25.766
Yes, sir! Of course!

20:26.725 --> 20:27.809
And finally...

20:29.061 --> 20:29.895
Eren.

20:34.233 --> 20:35.943
Hey, wait!

20:36.693 --> 20:38.153
Wait up!

20:39.780 --> 20:41.281
Don't you come in here!

20:42.407 --> 20:45.994
You're freaking kidding me.
You've got to be freaking kidding me.

20:46.411 --> 20:48.705
I'd be drinking right now
if it wasn't for you!

20:49.289 --> 20:51.124
This is all your fault!

20:51.500 --> 20:53.210
Stand back, rookies.

20:54.670 --> 20:55.671
Leave it to us.

20:56.880 --> 20:59.007
It's time to show off our ODM gear.

21:01.677 --> 21:02.928
Let's go!

21:20.779 --> 21:22.322
And finally, Eren.

21:23.156 --> 21:24.866
Learn how to restrain yourself.

21:26.576 --> 21:28.870
Don't succumb to rage
and lose sight of the goal.

21:30.080 --> 21:31.707
We can't afford another mistake.

21:32.708 --> 21:33.542
Yes, sir!

21:36.336 --> 21:38.714
There's a tower nearby
where we can assess the wall.

21:39.965 --> 21:42.467
It's in an abandoned castle
to the southwest.

21:43.635 --> 21:45.637
We'll ride to Utgard Castle.

23:36.665 --> 23:39.835
While searching for the Titans' breach
in the wall,

23:40.252 --> 23:42.295
the Scouts arrive at Utgard Castle.

23:43.380 --> 23:45.507
Their break was cut short
by Titans who are moving

23:45.841 --> 23:49.010
even under the darkness of night.

23:50.345 --> 23:52.013
The Scouts fight back gallantly.

23:53.265 --> 23:57.227
As the Titans' invasion presses
within the castle,

23:57.519 --> 23:59.354
Reiner recollects a scene from his past.

24:00.647 --> 24:03.358
Next episode, "Soldier."
